---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import ScrollAreaDemo from '../../components/ScrollAreaDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Scroll Area"
  description="A scrolling region with thin, theme-aware scrollbars for lists, panels, and wide data grids."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Scroll Area</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A scrolling region with thin scrollbars that follow the theme. Fixed or content heights, vertical, horizontal, or
    both bars, and a bordered table frame for wide data grids.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ScrollAreaDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="ScrollArea usage"
      code={`import { ScrollArea } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/scroll-area";

<ScrollArea size="sm" viewportLabel="Recent activity">
  {records.map((record) => <p key={record.id}>{record.title}</p>)}
</ScrollArea>

<ScrollArea size="md" orientation="both" viewportLabel="Wide report">
  <div className="w-160">…</div>
</ScrollArea>

<ScrollArea
  variant="table"
  orientation="both"
  viewportLabel="Bulb plantings"
  data-slot="table-container"
>
  <table aria-label="Bulb plantings">…</table>
</ScrollArea>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>"sm"</code> (10rem tall) or <code>"md"</code> (16rem tall). Leave it out to follow the
      content or your <code>className</code>. <code>orientation</code> is <code>"vertical"</code> (default),
      <code>"horizontal"</code>, or <code>"both"</code>. Each bar appears only while its axis overflows, and the corner
      fills the gap when both show.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>variant="table"</code> adds a 1px input-tone border, rounded corners, and the surface color. It caps the
      viewport at <code>60dvh</code>
      and gives it <code>role="region"</code>, named by <code>viewportLabel</code>. A sticky <code>thead</code> inside
      it stays pinned while rows scroll. Pass the table's own <code>aria-label</code> as <code>viewportLabel</code>.
      Other root props, such as <code>data-slot</code>, pass through to the root.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">ScrollBar</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="ScrollBar usage"
      code={`import { ScrollBar } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/scroll-area";

<ScrollBar orientation="horizontal" className="my-bar" />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>ScrollArea</code> draws its bars for you. <code>ScrollBar</code> is the same 10px track and pill thumb,
      exported for custom Base UI scroll area compositions. It takes Base UI scrollbar props, and <code>className</code>
      may be a state function.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Scrolling stays native, so wheel, trackpad, touch, and keyboard all work. When content overflows, the viewport
      joins the Tab order and shows a focus ring; arrow keys, Page Up, Page Down, Home, and End then scroll it. When
      nothing overflows it leaves the Tab order. The bars are hidden from screen readers. Thumb color changes take 120ms
      and stop when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Thumbs use <code>--sprout-muted</code> at 40%, and 60% on hover or while scrolling. The table frame uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-input</code> and <code>--sprout-surface</code>. Focus uses <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
